{
  "_comment": "OPTIONAL authed usage readers, per surface. Map a surface -> a shell command that prints exactly ONE integer 0-100 = percent headroom remaining. The fleet runs it and uses the result as that surface's headroom, overriding quota-axi / the blind default. This is the sanctioned way to get real numbers for surfaces whose usage is NOT locally observable (cursor, cline): YOU supply a command that reads your own token from its local store and calls the provider's usage endpoint. The command OWNS all secret handling (read the token from a 0600 file; never put it on argv). Copy this to config/quota-overrides.json (gitignored) and fill in. Empty string or missing key = blind / fail-open (the default). Example (illustrative only — endpoint/parse are yours to verify): \"cline\": \"my-cline-usage-reader.sh\"",
  "cursor": "",
  "cline": ""
}
